## patel.codes/proofs — self-organizing swarm

**Work without a shadow.** There is no dedicated
coordinator. In an authorized sixteen-station swarm,
two stations retain producer responsibility, two retain
consumer responsibility, and twelve negotiate flex
work. These are working owners, not managers. Confirm
live identities and accepted roles; do not spawn extra
persistent stations or infer acceptance from delivery.

**Negotiate bounded ownership.** Before starting, agree
on the exact unit, owner, boundaries, dependencies,
budget, and stopping condition. Check existing leases.
Select and refill within USER authority; transfer only
to an accepting owner. Flex roles change at episode
boundaries. Preserve independent review. Escalate
unresolved conflicts, scope changes, budget increases,
and gate exceptions to the USER, not a new supervisor.

**Keep one assignment ledger.** Agree on its external
location and one temporary recorder. The recorder
serializes updates, not research decisions. Send compact
ownership and disposition receipts; obtain acknowledgment
before treating a lease as registered. Transfer recorder
duty explicitly. Supporting packets are not competing
queues. Preserve failed routes and reopening conditions.

**Follow the bottleneck.** Negotiate source extraction,
argument development, falsification, API feasibility,
implementation, or independent acceptance work. Delegate
only decision-changing questions; do not duplicate owned
work. Ready packets, not staffing quotas, justify more
consumers. No credible mechanisms justify research or
closure, not manufactured helpers. Release idle capacity.

**Serialize landing only.** Consumers agree on one
landing holder at a time, recorded and acknowledged
before integration. Bind the grant to the accepted
revision and exact reviewed artifact. Required gates
must pass before production integration. On stale state,
refresh canonically and revalidate affected closure
before renewing the grant. Release on receipt, failure,
or explicit transfer; never infer release from silence.
Do not move repository history manually.

**Assign verification, not supervision.** Name one
verifier per required gate. Independent acceptance and
a fresh adoption-side imported audit remain mandatory;
a producer audit does not replace them. The audit owner
is a bounded duty, not a coordinator session. Check
public signatures and transitive axioms, permitting only
`propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`. Preserve
exact source/dependency closure through adoption. Never
adopt audit Scratch or import Sorry into production.
Honor stricter USER gates; leave unpaid gates incomplete.

**Communicate decisions.** Monitor completion, changed
dependencies, contradictions, or a consequential stall,
not unchanged heartbeats. Assignment is not runtime
liveness; delivery is not consumption. Use bound receipts
rather than repeating adequate unchanged checks. Yield
when downstream owners have the work. Stop at closure
or budget; leave exact artifacts, ownership, unpaid
implications, and concrete reopening conditions.
